{"id":101,"explanation":"Do not cache get_user’s result for the lifetime of a process: a user’s roles could remain stale after they are revoked. get_user fetches the user identified by uid from the database. #640 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"Check db.Query’s error before scheduling rows.Close(). When the query fails, rows is nil, so closing it would be invalid. The comment applies to the query, error check, and deferred close.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"The zero-delay setTimeout schedules measure(el) after layout has had a chance to settle. The comment says queueMicrotask would run too early for that measurement.","unsure":""}
{"id":104,"explanation":"Never log the contents of the token’s Secret<String> value. Its Debug output must show a redacted value rather than the secret. Secret<String> is the token’s type.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"Keep the RetryCount constant and the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json in sync: changing either requires changing the other. appsettings.json is the configuration file, and Http.Retry is the referenced setting.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"The offset passed to ch.map must be divisible by pageSize, leaving no remainder. The memory mapping operation rejects offsets that are not page aligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"The trailing slash on the rsync source build/ makes rsync copy the contents of build into $DEST, rather than copying the build directory itself. $DEST is the destination variable.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The BRIN index on created_at is chosen for size: the comment says it is about 1% the size of a B-tree index. That choice relies on events being appended in time order. created_at is the indexed column.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"Replace this loop, which waits by repeatedly checking flag, with a futex-based wait. The stated completion condition is that lock_acquire in src/sync/lock.c sleeps while waiting; the path identifies the source file and lock_acquire the function.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"The reason dbo.RebuildStats runs on the secondary is documented at the failover anchor of the runbook. doc:runbook#failover is a documentation pointer; dbo.RebuildStats is the procedure being defined.","unsure":"The notation does not give the runbook document’s file path or location."}
{"id":111,"explanation":"Keep this timeout below 60 seconds because the upstream proxy terminates idle requests after 60 seconds. The assigned value, 30, satisfies that limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"Keep Widget’s destructor virtual. If it becomes non-virtual, deleting a derived object through a Widget pointer can skip the derived destructor. #915 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"Enable SQLite foreign-key enforcement before writing anything on this connection. The PRAGMA setting applies separately to each connection, so enabling it elsewhere is insufficient.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"Use the fixed-size ShortString form for Name because the containing record is written to disk byte for byte. Replacing it with string would change the record’s stored representation.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"Treat p_id as caller input and pass it as a bound value, as the USING p_id clause does for placeholder :1. Concatenating caller input into an EXECUTE IMMEDIATE SQL string would allow SQL injection.","unsure":""}
